---
import Base from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
const crumbs = [{ title: "Seasonal home care" }];
const seasons = [
  { id: "spring", name: "Spring", cue: "After cold or wet weather", question: "What changed since winter?", steps: [
    "From the ground, note overflow marks, displaced downspouts, or water pooling beside the home after rain.",
    "Look indoors for new stains, musty odors, or damp spots; document changes rather than guessing the cause.",
    "Review cooling equipment instructions and book professional service if your manufacturer recommends it."
  ], next: [{ href: "/tools/gutter-care-planner/", label: "Record drainage observations" }, { href: "/guides/spotting-moisture-early/", label: "Recognize early moisture signs" }] },
  { id: "summer", name: "Summer", cue: "Heat, storms, and humidity", question: "Which exposures affect this home?", steps: [
    "Check local heat and storm alerts; prioritize household preparedness before discretionary projects.",
    "Record indoor condensation or dampness and address persistent moisture with appropriate professional help.",
    "Check the actual HVAC manual for filter inspection guidance; do not assume a universal replacement interval."
  ], next: [{ href: "/guides/summer-maintenance-priorities/", label: "Read summer priority decision guide" }, { href: "/tools/climate-home-care/", label: "Select climate exposures" }, { href: "/tools/hvac-filter-schedule/", label: "Plan manual-based filter checks" }] },
  { id: "fall", name: "Fall", cue: "Before colder or wetter conditions", question: "What needs attention before the weather shifts?", steps: [
    "From safe ground level, note blocked-looking outlets, overflowing gutters, and drainage concerns; arrange qualified help for elevated work.",
    "Review doors and windows for drafts or visible deterioration, and check product instructions before sealing anything.",
    "Review heating equipment service guidance and household emergency contacts ahead of local severe-weather season."
  ], next: [{ href: "/tools/gutter-care-planner/", label: "Create a gutter follow-up list" }, { href: "/calculators/caulk-tube-estimator/", label: "Estimate sealant for an appropriate project" }] },
  { id: "winter", name: "Winter", cue: "Freezing conditions and indoor time", question: "Is the household prepared for local hazards?", steps: [
    "Monitor official local warnings and plan for heat or power interruptions; never run fuel-burning generators indoors.",
    "Note condensation, leaks, and indoor moisture; document recurring problems for a qualified professional.",
    "Review the maintenance log, manufacturer manuals, and next-year priorities instead of scheduling unsafe outdoor work."
  ], next: [{ href: "/guides/winter-home-observations/", label: "Read the winter observation checklist" }, { href: "/tools/maintenance-log/", label: "Update your maintenance records" }, { href: "/maintenance-calendar/", label: "Adjust your annual plan" }] }
];
---
<Base title="Seasonal Home Maintenance Guide and Planning Hub" description="A practical four-season home care guide: what to observe, what to prioritize, and which free planning tools to use for your own climate." breadcrumbs={crumbs}>
  <section class="page-head"><div class="container"><Breadcrumbs items={crumbs}/><span class="eyebrow">A HOMEOWNER'S FIELD GUIDE</span><h1>Care for your home, <em class="serif" style="color:var(--pine)">season by season.</em></h1><p class="lede">Start with the weather and systems your home actually has. Use this four-season field guide to spot changes, organize safe follow-up, and open the right planner—not to follow a one-size-fits-all repair schedule.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section-small rule-top"><div class="container">
    <div class="note"><strong>How to use this hub:</strong> Start with the season that matches your local conditions, not just the calendar month. For each observation, note what changed, consult equipment manuals and local alerts, and call a qualified professional for roofs, ladders, electrical, gas, structural or other hazardous work.</div>
    <nav class="season-nav" aria-label="Jump to a season">{seasons.map(s => <a href={"#"+s.id}>{s.name} ↓</a>)}</nav>
    {seasons.map((s,i) => <section class="season" id={s.id} aria-labelledby={s.id+"-title"}>
      <span class="eyebrow">{String(i+1).padStart(2,"0")} / {s.cue}</span>
      <h2 id={s.id+"-title"}>{s.name}: {s.question}</h2>
      <ul>{s.steps.map(step => <li>{step}</li>)}</ul>
      <div class="season-links"><strong>Take the next step</strong>{s.next.map(n => <a href={n.href}>{n.label} ↗</a>)}</div>
    </section>)}
  </div></section>
  <section class="section-small rule-top"><div class="container">
    <h2>Build a plan that fits your home</h2>
    <p>A seasonal overview helps you decide where to look. For an actual checklist, use the <a href="/tools/seasonal-maintenance-builder/">seasonal maintenance builder</a> to choose your home systems and broad climate conditions. For recurring tasks across all twelve months, open the <a href="/maintenance-calendar/">annual maintenance calendar</a>. Keep completed work in the <a href="/tools/maintenance-log/">private maintenance log</a>.</p>
    <h2>Sources and limits</h2>
    <p>Seasonal timing differs by U.S. region, elevation, weather, building type, and equipment. These are observation and planning prompts, not universal inspection intervals or instructions for dangerous repairs. Consult <a href="https://www.ready.gov/winter-weather">FEMA Ready.gov winter weather guidance</a> for preparedness, <a href="https://www.epa.gov/mold/brief-guide-mold-moisture-and-your-home">EPA moisture guidance</a> for persistent dampness, and <a href="https://www.energy.gov/energysaver/maintaining-your-air-conditioner">DOE air-conditioner maintenance guidance</a> for equipment context. Use the manufacturer's manual and local emergency instructions for your actual situation.</p>
    <p class="small muted">Published by Upkeep Atlas · November 8, 2026 · Editorial research and automated checks; no professional inspection or expert review is claimed.</p>
  </div></section>
  <style>
    .season-nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem;margin:2rem 0 1rem}
    .season-nav a{display:inline-block;padding:.6rem .85rem;border:1px solid currentColor;text-decoration:none}
    .season{padding:2.25rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line,#ccc);scroll-margin-top:2rem}
    .season h2{max-width:52rem;margin:.65rem 0 1rem}
    .season ul{max-width:52rem;line-height:1.7;padding-left:1.5rem}
    .season li{margin:.6rem 0}
    .season-links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:.8rem 1.5rem;margin-top:1.4rem}
    .season-links a{color:var(--pine);text-underline-offset:.2rem}
    :global([data-theme="dark"]) .season-links a{color:inherit}
    a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid currentColor;outline-offset:4px}
    @media(max-width:480px){.season-links{display:grid;gap:.7rem}}
    @media print{.season-nav,.season-links{display:none}.season{break-inside:avoid}}
  </style>
</Base>
